window.WIKI = {"built":"2026-11-19","home":{"title":"Own A World Player Wiki","lead":"Prices, recipes and rules for Own A World, written from the game's own data. Pick a page, or search for what you need."},"groups":[{"name":"Basics","pages":["getting-started","worlds-and-building","commands","faq"]},{"name":"Guides","pages":["how-to-get-things","recipes"]},{"name":"Activities","pages":["farming-and-splicing","fishing"]},{"name":"Economy","pages":["gems-and-trading"]},{"name":"Seasonal","pages":["events","whats-new"]}],"quick":[{"label":"What do the controls do?","page":"getting-started","anchor":"controls"},{"label":"How much is a World Lock?","page":"worlds-and-building","anchor":"locks"},{"label":"Where do I get a Kitchen Oven?","page":"how-to-get-things","anchor":"things-you-make-or-find"},{"label":"What are the splice recipes?","page":"recipes","anchor":"splice-recipes"},{"label":"How do I splice seeds?","page":"farming-and-splicing","anchor":"splicing-making-new-seeds"},{"label":"What is Farmer's Illness?","page":"farming-and-splicing","anchor":"farmers-illness"},{"label":"Which fishing rod should I use?","page":"fishing","anchor":"rods"},{"label":"How do I trade safely?","page":"gems-and-trading","anchor":"trading"},{"label":"What does each gem pack cost?","page":"gems-and-trading","anchor":"buying-gems-with-robux"},{"label":"What commands can I use?","page":"commands","anchor":"social-and-travel"}],"order":["getting-started","worlds-and-building","commands","faq","how-to-get-things","recipes","farming-and-splicing","fishing","gems-and-trading","events","whats-new"],"pages":{"getting-started":{"title":"Getting Started","nav":"Getting started","summary":"Welcome to Own A World. You build, farm and trade in worlds of your own. Every world is its own space, so what you build there stays yours once you lock it.","md":"# Getting Started\n\nWelcome to Own A World. You build, farm and trade in worlds of your own. Every world is its own space, so what you build there stays yours once you lock it.\n\n## Your first minutes\n1. **Play the tutorial.** New players start in a private tutorial world with a guide. It teaches walking, breaking blocks, planting and harvesting, building, and splicing seeds. Each lesson pays a few gems, and you can skip it or replay it later from Settings.\n2. **Follow the Getting Started goals** in the top left after the tutorial. Each goal teaches one thing and pays gems. The goals walk you through making your own world, locking it, and spending your first gems in the Store.\n3. **Make your own world.** Open **Worlds**, type a name nobody has used, and press Go. Any free name is yours to claim.\n\n## The idea of the game\n\n<!--fig-loop-->\n<figure class=\"fig fig-flow\" aria-label=\"The game loop: break, collect, plant, splice, lock and build\">\n<p class=\"fig-title\">The game loop</p>\n<div class=\"fig-row\">\n<div class=\"step\">{{icon:item-pickaxe}}<b>Break blocks</b><span>Punch blocks to get gems, seeds and blocks.</span></div>\n<div class=\"step\">{{icon:item-dirt-seed}}<b>Collect seeds</b><span>Walk over drops to pick them up.</span></div>\n<div class=\"step\">{{icon:tree-poplar}}<b>Plant and grow</b><span>Plant a seed above a solid block and wait.</span></div>\n<div class=\"step\">{{icon:item-blackrock-wall-seed}}<b>Splice</b><span>Use a second seed on a growing tree for a new one.</span></div>\n<div class=\"step\">{{icon:item-world-lock}}<b>Lock and build</b><span>Lock your world, then build what you like.</span></div>\n</div>\n</figure>\n\nPunch blocks, collect seeds, plant them, harvest trees full of blocks, and splice seeds to discover new ones. Lock your world so only you and the friends you choose can build, then build whatever you like.\n\n## Controls\n\n<!--fig-keys-->\n<figure class=\"fig\" aria-label=\"Keyboard controls\">\n<p class=\"fig-title\">Keyboard at a glance</p>\n<div class=\"keys\">\n<div class=\"keyrow\"><div class=\"caps\"><span class=\"cap\">A</span><span class=\"cap\">D</span></div><span>Move left and right (arrow keys also work)</span></div>\n<div class=\"keyrow\"><div class=\"caps\"><span class=\"cap\">W</span><span class=\"cap\">Space</span></div><span>Jump (the Up arrow also works)</span></div>\n<div class=\"keyrow\"><div class=\"caps\"><span class=\"cap\">E</span></div><span>Open your inventory</span></div>\n<div class=\"keyrow\"><div class=\"caps\"><span class=\"cap\">B</span></div><span>Open the Store</span></div>\n<div class=\"keyrow\"><div class=\"caps\"><span class=\"cap\">1</span><span class=\"cap\">2</span><span class=\"cap\">3</span><span class=\"cap\">4</span></div><span>Pick a quickbar slot (slot 1 swaps Fist and Wrench)</span></div>\n<div class=\"keyrow\"><div class=\"caps\"><span class=\"cap\">Enter</span></div><span>Chat</span></div>\n</div>\n</figure>\n\n| Action | Keyboard | Phone or tablet |\n|---|---|---|\n| Move | A / D or the arrow keys | On-screen arrows |\n| Jump | W, Up arrow or Space | Jump button |\n| Punch, break, harvest | Click or hold on a nearby block | Tap or hold a nearby block |\n| Place a block, plant a seed | Select it, then click an empty tile within reach | Select it, then tap |\n| Inventory | E, or the button beside the quickbar | Inventory button |\n| Store | B | Menu, then Shop |\n| Chat | Enter | Chat button |\n\n- **Hold to keep punching.** Extra clicking does not break blocks faster.\n- **Quickbar:** four slots near the bottom. Keys 1 to 4 select them. Slot 1 always holds your **Fist** and **Wrench**; click it to swap.\n- **Fist** breaks blocks and harvests trees. **Wrench** configures things (locks, doors, chests, other players).\n- **Mobile controls** can be moved and resized in Settings, with a left-handed preset.\n\n## Gems, levels and daily rewards\n- **Gems** come from breaking blocks, harvesting, missions and level-ups.\n- **Missions:** Daily and Weekly missions pay gems, plus a bonus for finishing every mission in a set. They are the steadiest way to earn early on.\n- **Levels:** you gain XP from what you do. Each level pays a gem reward, and every fifth level pays double.\n- **Daily login:** each day you come back pays more, up to a seven-day ladder, and a longer streak adds a bonus on top.\n\n## Staying safe\n- **Lock your world first.** Anything on unlocked land can be broken by visitors, and items dropped on the ground can be picked up by anyone.\n- **Use the trade window** for every trade. Never give items away for a promise.\n- **Report problems** from the Menu (Report World) or the player menu. For anything serious, also use Report in the Roblox menu.\n\n## Where next\n[Worlds, locks and building](#worlds-and-building) · [Farming and splicing](#farming-and-splicing) · [Fishing](#fishing) · [How to get things](#how-to-get-things) · [Recipes](#recipes) · [Gems and trading](#gems-and-trading)\n"},"worlds-and-building":{"title":"Worlds and Building","nav":"Worlds and building","summary":"## Making and claiming a world Open Worlds, type a new name and press Go. A world with a free name is yours to claim, but unlocked land can be changed by anyone, so...","md":"# Worlds and Building\n\n## Making and claiming a world\nOpen **Worlds**, type a new name and press Go. A world with a free name is yours to claim, but unlocked land can be changed by anyone, so claim it with a lock.\n\n## Locks\n\n<!--fig-locks-->\n<figure class=\"fig\" aria-label=\"How much land each lock protects\">\n<p class=\"fig-title\">How much each lock protects</p>\n<div class=\"hbars\">\n<div class=\"hrow\"><div class=\"nm\">{{icon:item-small-lock}}Small Lock</div><div class=\"track\"><i style=\"width:5%\"></i></div><div class=\"val\">10 tiles</div></div>\n<div class=\"hrow\"><div class=\"nm\">{{icon:item-big-lock}}Big Lock</div><div class=\"track\"><i style=\"width:24%\"></i></div><div class=\"val\">48 tiles</div></div>\n<div class=\"hrow\"><div class=\"nm\">{{icon:item-huge-lock}}Huge Lock</div><div class=\"track\"><i style=\"width:60%\"></i></div><div class=\"val\">200 tiles</div></div>\n<div class=\"hrow\"><div class=\"nm\">{{icon:item-world-lock}}World Lock</div><div class=\"track\"><i style=\"width:100%\"></i></div><div class=\"val\">Whole world</div></div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"fig-note\">Bars show relative size. The Small, Big and Huge Locks guard an area inside a world. The World Lock guards all of it.</p>\n</figure>\n\nA lock makes land yours. Wrench your lock to manage who can build.\n\n| Lock | Protects | Store price |\n|---|---|---|\n| {{icon:item-world-lock}} **World Lock** | The whole world | 2,000 gems |\n| {{icon:item-small-lock}} Small Lock | Up to 10 tiles | 100 gems |\n| {{icon:item-big-lock}} Big Lock | Up to 48 tiles | 250 gems |\n| {{icon:item-huge-lock}} Huge Lock | Up to 200 tiles | 500 gems |\n\n- Prices and stock can change. The Store always shows the current price.\n- Only invite people you trust. Friends you add can build in your locked area.\n- **Weather machines** need a World Lock before you can place them.\n- Your first lock is free in the tutorial (the Starter World Lock) and in the Getting Started goals.\n\n## Doors, chests and seats\n- **Treasure Chest** (500 gems): wrench it to open 27 storage slots. Drag stacks in and out, or use Take All and Leave All. Empty a chest before you break it. You can share access with one other player.\n- **House Entrance** (150 gems): a door that anyone with build access walks through. Everyone else bumps into it.\n- **Travel doors** can be set to lead to another world. Wrench one to set its destination, then stand inside and punch it with your Fist to go through.\n- **Seats:** stand still in front of a chair for three seconds to sit.\n- **Main Door:** the entrance to your world. The **Door Mover** (5,000 gems, single use) lets a World Lock owner move it.\n- **Change of Address** (20,000 gems, single use) renames your locked world to a new, unused name.\n\n## Water and hazards\n- Use a **Water Bucket** on a tile to add water, and on existing water to scoop it away (you usually get the bucket back).\n- Watch out for lava and stinging jellyfish. Keep a safe route home when exploring. If you get stuck, use **Respawn** in the Menu.\n\n## Protecting your world\n| Item | What it does | Price |\n|---|---|---|\n| {{icon:item-punch-jammer}} Punch Jammer | Stops punches and knockback from other players. Block breaking still works. | 15,000 gems |\n| {{icon:item-signal-jammer}} Signal Jammer | Hides your world from public listings and hides its name in broadcasts. | 2,000 gems |\n| {{icon:item-zombie-jammer}} Zombie Jammer | Stops infection from zombie bites. | 15,000 gems |\n| {{icon:item-jump-jammer}} Jump Jammer | Stops double jumping in your world. | 10,000 gems |\n| {{icon:item-anti-gravity-generator}} Anti Gravity Generator | Everyone falls slowly and can jump as much as they like. | 450,000 gems |\n\n## Weather\nThe most recently switched-on weather machine sets the sky, and only one runs at a time.\n\n<figure class=\"fig\" aria-label=\"Weather machines and prices\">\n<p class=\"fig-title\">Weather machines</p>\n<div class=\"gallery\">\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:item-sunny-weather-machine}}<b>Sunny</b><span>1,000 gems</span></div>\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:item-night-weather-machine}}<b>Night</b><span>10,000 gems</span></div>\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:item-arid-weather-machine}}<b>Arid</b><span>10,000 gems</span></div>\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:item-rainy-city-weather-machine}}<b>Rainy City</b><span>10,000 gems</span></div>\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:item-warp-speed-weather-machine}}<b>Warp Speed</b><span>10,000 gems</span></div>\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:item-jungle-weather-machine}}<b>Jungle</b><span>20,000 gems</span></div>\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:item-storm-weather-machine}}<b>Storm</b><span>25,000 gems</span></div>\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:item-digital-rain-weather-machine}}<b>Digital Rain</b><span>30,000 gems. One per world.</span></div>\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:item-item-rain-weather-machine}}<b>Item Rain</b><span>50,000 gems. One per world.</span></div>\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:item-infinity-weather-machine}}<b>Infinity</b><span>50,000 gems</span></div>\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:item-backdrop-weather-machine}}<b>Backdrop</b><span>150,000 gems. One per world.</span></div>\n</div>\n</figure>\n\n- **Storm worlds:** every so often lightning strikes the highest player. It can knock them out. A lucky strike on someone carrying a **Sky Bottle** turns it into a **Riding Cloud**.\n- **Infinity Weather Machine:** load it with your other machines and it cycles through them on a timer.\n\n## Theme packs\nThe Store sells theme packs that give you a set of blocks and outfit pieces for one style, such as Fishing, Parkour, Fantasy, Dungeon, School, Farm, City, Wild West and more. Packs can include a chance at a bonus rare piece.\n\n## Building tips\n- Lock first, build second.\n- Open your inventory with **E**, select a block, then click or tap an empty tile within reach.\n- Clothes are worn from the backpack's **INFO**, or by double-clicking them.\n- The **+** at the end of your inventory buys more backpack space. Each upgrade costs more.\n- The **World Planner** helps you lay out a build before you place blocks.\n"},"commands":{"title":"Commands","nav":"Commands","summary":"Type a command in chat. Press Enter to open chat, then type the command and press Enter again. Type /help in the game for the current list.","md":"# Commands\n\nType a command in chat. Press **Enter** to open chat, then type the command and press Enter again. Type **/help** in the game for the current list.\n\n## Social and travel\n| Command | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| /msg &lt;name&gt; &lt;text&gt; | Send a private message to a player in any world. Use /r &lt;text&gt; to reply. |\n| /warp &lt;world&gt; | Go straight to a world. Supporter and up. |\n| /sb &lt;text&gt; | Super broadcast: tell every world. It costs 40 gems per player online in every server, and the game shows the price first. |\n| /who | List everyone in this world. |\n| /trade &lt;name&gt; | Send a trade request to a player in this world. |\n| /top | The most honored worlds today, yesterday and overall. /top today 2 shows page 2. |\n| /honors | This world's honors. |\n\n## For world owners and people with access\n| Command | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| /pull &lt;name&gt; | Bring a player to you. Part of any of their names works. |\n| /kick &lt;name&gt; | Knock a player out. They respawn at the door or their checkpoint. |\n| /ban &lt;name&gt; | Ban a player from your world for 1 hour. |\n| /uba | Unban everyone in your world. World owner only. |\n| /unaccess | Remove your own access from every lock in this world. |\n| /sethome | Make a world you own your home world. |\n\n## Emotes\nMoves and poses you can play with a command.\n- **Loop until you move:** /dance, /dance2, /dab, /march, /sleep\n- **Expressions:** /smile, /laugh, /wave, /love, /cry, /sad, /mad, /wink, /yes, /no, /cheer, /omg\n- **More:** /troll, /shy, /shrug, /fp, /foldarms, /rolleyes, /grumpy, /furious, /mog\n- **Faces in chat:** typing `:)` `:D` `;)` `:(` `:p` `:*` `:o` `-_-` or `0-0` plays the matching emote.\n- **/smooth:** a stage routine. Wear the full Smooth Criminal set.\n- **/supersayan:** a Super Saiyan transformation. Wear the Spiky Hero Hair.\n\n## Tips\n- Names do not need to be exact. A full name wins over the start of a name, and the start of a name wins over part of one. If several players match equally well, use more of the name.\n- Ordinary chat stays inside your current world. Use /msg or /sb to reach other worlds.\n"},"faq":{"title":"FAQ","nav":"FAQ","summary":"Short answers to common questions, with a link to the page that has the full story.","md":"# FAQ\n\nShort answers to common questions, with a link to the page that has the full story.\n\n## Farming and drops\n**Why are my drops getting smaller?** You may have Farmer's Illness. After about 2 hours of active farming, rewards fall fast. Take a 15 minute break to cure it. See [Farming and splicing](#farming-and-splicing).\n\n**Why did my trees change?** There are now 12 kinds of tree, chosen by the item the seed grows. This is a change to how trees look.\n\n## Worlds\n**Why can't I place a weather machine?** Weather machines need a World Lock in the world first. See [Worlds and building](#worlds-and-building).\n\n**How do I move my world's entrance?** Buy a Door Mover (a single-use item) and use it in your own locked world.\n\n**How do I rename my world?** A Change of Address (single use) gives your locked world a new, unused name.\n\n**Someone is griefing my world.** Lock it. Anything on unlocked land can be broken by visitors. You can also use /ban or /kick if you own it. See [Commands](#commands).\n\n## Fishing\n**Why can't I cast?** The water must be part of a pool at least 2 tiles wide and 2 deep, you must stand on the ground and wear a rod, and your rod must not be worn out. You also cannot fish if you are seasick after about 1.5 hours of fishing. See [Fishing](#fishing).\n\n**Where do I repair my rod?** At a Fishing Hut's Workbench, for gems.\n\n## Money and trading\n**Why can't I trade?** You need level 10, and trades have extra account checks. Both of you must be in the same world. See [Gems and trading](#gems-and-trading).\n\n**Where is the gift someone sent me?** Gifts wait in your gift box and arrive when you join, or right away if you are in the same server.\n\n**What is a Birth Certificate?** It lets you choose your in-game name. Use 3 to 20 letters and numbers with at least one letter. Your first one is free, and you need an open backpack slot to claim it.\n\n**What do Supporter passes give me?** Extra backpack slots, gems, a bonus on gem packs, extra skin colours and more XP. See [Gems and trading](#gems-and-trading).\n\n## Interface\n**How do I hide the screen's buttons?** Tap the eye button in the chat tools row. Tap the eye in the same place to bring them back.\n\n**Can I move the touch controls?** Yes. Open Settings and choose Customize controls. There is a left-handed preset.\n\n**The Wardrobe says it is turned off.** That is true for now. Wear clothes from your backpack with INFO, or by double-clicking them.\n\n**Is there voice chat?** If your Roblox account has voice chat, a microphone button appears in the chat tools row.\n\n## Help\n**Where is the Beginner's Book?** Open the Menu and choose Beginner's Book.\n\n**How do I report a player or a world?** Use Report World in the Menu, or Report in the player menu. For anything serious, also use Report in the Roblox menu (Esc or the Roblox button).\n"},"how-to-get-things":{"title":"How to get things","nav":"How to get things","summary":"Where each item comes from, and what it costs. The Store is the main shop. Prices are in gems and can change, so check the price shown in the Store before you buy....","md":"# How to get things\n\nWhere each item comes from, and what it costs. The Store is the main shop. Prices are in gems and can change, so check the price shown in the Store before you buy. For recipes see [Recipes](#recipes).\n\n## The ways to get items\n| Way | What you get there |\n|---|---|\n| **Store** | Locks, seed packs, theme packs, clothing packs, jammers, weather machines, the Geiger Counter and the Item of the Month |\n| **Splicing** | Many blocks, furniture, appliances and some wings. See [Recipes](#recipes) |\n| **Chemical Combiner** | Lab clothes and a few lab items. See [Recipes](#recipes) |\n| **Fishing** | Fish, bait, rods and the rare Sky Bottle. See [Fishing](#fishing) |\n| **Digging** | Treasure from a Geiger Counter |\n| **Events** | Festival and seasonal items. See [Events](#events) |\n| **Other players** | Trades, vending machines and auctions. See [Gems and trading](#gems-and-trading) |\n\n## Buying in the Store\n\n### World and building gear\n| Item | Price | What it does |\n|---|---|---|\n| {{icon:item-world-lock}} World Lock | 2,000 gems | Locks a whole world |\n| {{icon:item-small-lock}} Small Lock | 100 gems | Locks 10 tiles |\n| {{icon:item-big-lock}} Big Lock | 250 gems | Locks 48 tiles |\n| {{icon:item-huge-lock}} Huge Lock | 500 gems | Locks 200 tiles |\n| {{icon:item-growth-mist}} Growth Mist (5) | 200 gems | Each bottle removes 1 hour of tree growth |\n| {{icon:item-deluxe-growth-mist}} Deluxe Growth Mist | 900 gems | Removes 24 hours of growth |\n| {{icon:item-treasure-chest}} Treasure Chest | 500 gems | Storage |\n| {{icon:item-vending-machine}} Vending Machine | 8,000 gems | Sells items for World Locks |\n| {{icon:item-seed-vending-machine}} Seed Vending Machine | 500 gems | Sells items for seeds |\n| House Entrance | 150 gems | A door for builders |\n| {{icon:item-door-mover}} Door Mover | 5,000 gems | Moves your Main Door once |\n| {{icon:item-punch-jammer}} Punch Jammer | 15,000 gems | Stops punches and knockback |\n| {{icon:item-signal-jammer}} Signal Jammer | 2,000 gems | Hides your world from public lists |\n| {{icon:item-zombie-jammer}} Zombie Jammer | 15,000 gems | Stops zombie bites infecting |\n| {{icon:item-jump-jammer}} Jump Jammer | 10,000 gems | Stops double jumping |\n| {{icon:item-anti-gravity-generator}} Anti Gravity Generator | 450,000 gems | Lowers gravity |\n| Weather machines | 1,000 to 150,000 gems | See [Worlds and building](#worlds-and-building) |\n\n### You and your account\n| Item | Price | What it does |\n|---|---|---|\n| {{icon:item-backpack}} More Inventory | From 100 gems | +10 backpack slots each time, up to 396 slots |\n| Birth Certificate | 17,500 gems | Changes your name once every 30 days |\n| {{icon:item-change-of-address}} Change of Address | 20,000 gems | Renames a locked world |\n\n### Seeds and packs\n| Pack | Price | What you get |\n|---|---|---|\n| Basic Seed Pack | 100 gems | 5 random common seeds |\n| Basic Splicing Kit | 150 gems | 5 random starter seeds |\n| Rare Seed Pack | 1,000 gems | 5 random seeds from over 120 kinds |\n| Starter Farmables Pack | 3,000 gems, once a day | 6 bundles of 6 seeds (Sugar Cane, Blackrock Wall, Venus Flytrap, Fish Tank) |\n| Hat Pack | 600 gems | 1 random hat |\n| Clothes Pack | 400 gems | 3 random everyday clothes |\n| Rare Clothes Pack | 1,000 gems | 3 random rare wearables |\n| Girl Hair Pack and Boy Hair Pack | 500 gems each | 1 random hairstyle |\n| Fashion packs (Y2K, Emo & Goth, Streetwear, Cozy and more) | 1,400 gems each | 1 random piece in that style, in a women's and a men's version |\n\n### Rare items\n| Item | Price | Where |\n|---|---|---|\n| Abyssal Wings | 75,000 gems | **Item of the Month** in the Featured tab, while it is featured |\n| Angel Wings | 20,000 gems | Featured tab, limited time with a countdown |\n| Tiny Bat Wings | 15,000 gems | Featured tab, limited time with a countdown |\n| Red Dragon | 50,000 gems | Special tab |\n| Fusion Hoverboard | 30,000 gems | Special tab |\n| Geiger Counter | 25,000 gems | World Stuff tab. It is **only sold here** |\n| Pet Slime | 100,000 gems | A pet that spits acid when you punch, digs 1.5x faster and makes you jump 15% higher |\n| Pocket Pony | 25,000 gems | A tiny horse you ride for extra speed on land |\n| Mars Blast, Undersea Worldseed, Jungle Worldseed | 15,000 gems each | Each makes a **new** themed world with an unused name. Bring a World Lock |\n| Thermonuclear Blast | 15,000 gems | Makes a new, completely cleared world. Bring a World Lock |\n\n## Theme packs: what is inside\nEach theme pack is a bundle of blocks and an outfit, and many have a small chance of a bonus rare piece. Some of what is in them is hard to get any other way.\n\n| Pack | Price | Notable items |\n|---|---|---|\n| {{icon:item-fishing-hut}} Fishing Hut | 1,000 gems | The hut alone |\n| Fishin' Pack | 3,000 gems | Fishing Hut, Fishing Rod, bait, Fishbowl, Fish Tank Port |\n| Home Pack | 5,000 gems | {{icon:item-kitchen-oven}} Kitchen Oven, Microwave, Television, Bed, Toilet, Couch |\n| {{icon:item-farm-tractor}} Farm Pack | 15,000 gems | Cow (milk), Chicken (eggs), Farm Tractor, Wheat |\n| Wild West Pack | 8,000 gems | Bison (milk), Campfire, Hay Bale |\n| Zombie Defense Pack | 10,000 gems | Z-Strain, Antidote, Toxic Waste Barrel |\n| Astro Pack | 5,000 gems | Jetpack, Tesla Coil, Moonstone |\n| Vegas Pack | 8,000 gems | Neon Lights, Rainbow, Golden Block |\n| City Pack | 8,000 gems | Garbage, the start of the splice chain to Cutaway Building and Neon Outline Block |\n| Parkour Pack | 5,000 gems | Checkpoints, climbing walls, ladders, ice, spikes |\n| Dungeon Pack | 10,000 gems | Iron Block, Torch, Cobweb |\n| Racing Pack | 3,500 gems | Checkpoints, race flags, arrows |\n| Fantasy Pack | 5,000 gems | Treasure Chests, Cave Gateway, Wizard Hat |\n| School Pack | 5,000 gems | Pencils, Bookshelves, Textbooks |\n| Roaring Twenties Pack | 5,000 gems | Marble, Lamp Posts, Guitar |\n| Adventure Pack | 6,000 gems | Expedition props, gateways, death spikes |\n| Rockin' Pack | 9,999 gems | Guitar, Mohawk |\n| Cinema Pack | 6,000 gems | Cool Shades, Headphones |\n| Prehistoric Pack | 5,000 gems | Stone, Gravel, Leaves, Cave Gateway |\n| Shop Pack | 8,000 gems | Display Blocks, signs, Cash Register, Mannequin |\n| Sportsball Pack | 2,500 gems | Pitch, bleachers, goals |\n| Steampunk Pack | 4,000 gems | Top Hat, Tesla Coil, Iron Block, steam parts |\n\nThe **Mad Science Kit** holds the Laboratory, Science Stations and the chemicals used in the Chemical Combiner. It is not sold in the Store at the moment, so ask players who already own these items.\n\n## Things you make or find\n| Item | How to get it |\n|---|---|\n| {{icon:item-kitchen-oven}} Kitchen Oven | Splice Pocket Lighter and Air Duct seeds, or buy the Home Pack |\n| Microwave | Splice Toxic Waste Barrel and Television seeds, or buy the Home Pack |\n| Chemicals | A **Science Station** brews one every 2 to 3 hours. Wrench it to collect. Mysterious Chemical is a combiner recipe |\n| Boombox, Disco Ball | Splice. Boombox is Black and Steel Block. Disco Ball is Boombox and Window |\n| Fairy Wings | Splice Flowery Wallpaper and Disco Ball |\n| Crimson Eagle Wings | Splice Red Wallpaper and Blue Wallpaper |\n| Rainbow Wings | Splice Ruby Block and Emerald Block. The tree takes **120 days** to grow |\n| {{icon:item-sky-bottle}} Sky Bottle | A rare catch when fishing in a world with a Storm Weather Machine. Lightning can wake the cloud inside into a Riding Cloud |\n| {{icon:item-hand-scythe}} Hand Scythe | Festival combine. See [Recipes](#recipes) |\n| {{icon:item-harvest-scythe}} Harvest Scythe | A reward from the Offering Table. See [Events](#events) |\n| Golden Block | Splice Steel Block and Yellow |\n| Crystal Block | Almost never turns up. Smash a Golden Treasure Hoard in a Cave Worldseed world for a chance. It is the start of the Ruby, Emerald and Rainbow Wings chain |\n\n## Digging with a Geiger Counter\nHold a Geiger Counter and follow the rings to buried treasure in any world. You can dig up:\n- Gems and chests with more gems\n- Green, blue and red crystals (common), and white and black crystals (rare)\n- Pearls, Star Fuel, goo, Batteries and Chargers\n- Relics such as the Sunken Vase, Old Anchor, Stone Idol and Deep Iron\n- Junk: Old Boots, Tin Cans and Bottles\n\n## Other sources\n- **Daily login and level-ups** pay gems. See [Gems and trading](#gems-and-trading).\n- **World Tokens** come from the daily delivery quest and are spent in the token shop on items and XP Potions.\n- **Events** have their own rewards. See [Events](#events).\n- **Other players** sell on vending machines. Compare prices before you buy. See [Gems and trading](#gems-and-trading).\n"},"recipes":{"title":"Recipes","nav":"Recipes","summary":"Everything you can make, with the exact ingredients. Splice recipes, the Chemical Combiner and the festival combines are all here. For how splicing works, see...","md":"# Recipes\n\nEverything you can make, with the exact ingredients. Splice recipes, the Chemical Combiner and the festival combines are all here. For how splicing works, see [Farming and splicing](#farming-and-splicing).\n\n## Splice recipes\nPlant one seed and use the other on the same growing tree. **Either seed can go first.** Each row shows the two seeds to splice. A pair of seeds only ever makes one result. The tables list every recipe, so you can search for what you want to make.\n\n### Ground, stone and plants\n| You get | Splice these two |\n|---|---|\n| Grass | Dirt + Stone |\n| Sand | Gravel + Dirt |\n| Concrete | Gravel + Stone |\n| Wheat | Grass + Sand |\n| Sunflower | Grass + Gravel |\n| Daisy | Grass + Dirt |\n| Rose | Grass + Magma |\n| Cornflower | Glass Pane + Grass |\n| Cactus | Bush + Death Spikes |\n| Agaric Mushroom | Grass + Dirt BG |\n| Leaves | Wooden Log + Grass |\n| Hay Bale | Sunflower + Wooden Crate |\n| Brick Block | Stone + Grass |\n| Barn Block | Red + Wooden Block |\n| Stone BG | Stone + Wooden Door |\n| Mud Block | Dirt + Wooden BG |\n| Mossy Stone | Stone + Leaves |\n| Boulder | Gravel + Magma |\n| Marble | Concrete + White |\n| Sandstone | Cactus + Dirt |\n| Obsidian | Magma + Blue |\n| Snow Block | Ice + White |\n| Ice | Glass Pane + Cloudstone Block |\n| Cloud | Rainbow + Glass Block |\n| Moonstone | Bed + Wooden Ladder |\n| Neptune | Moonstone + Blue |\n| Cave Gateway | Gravel + Dirt BG |\n| Stalactite | Dark Cave BG + Death Spikes |\n| Dark Cave BG | Dirt BG + Black |\n\n### Wood and furniture\n| You get | Splice these two |\n|---|---|\n| Wooden Block | Magma + Dirt |\n| Wooden BG | Grass + Wooden Door |\n| Wooden Door | Dirt + Dirt BG |\n| Wooden Sign | Dirt BG + Stone |\n| Wooden Frame | Wooden Block + Dirt BG |\n| Wooden Log | Wooden Block + Wooden BG |\n| Wooden Platform | Wooden Block + Grass |\n| Wooden Chair | Wooden Log + Wooden Frame |\n| Wooden Table | Wooden Platform + Wooden Block |\n| Wooden Crate | Wooden Sign + Dirt |\n| Wooden Barrel | Wooden Crate + Wooden Log |\n| Wooden Ladder | Giant Up Arrow + Wooden Platform |\n| Wooden Fence | Wooden Chair + White |\n| Wooden Stair | Wooden Platform + Dungeon Door |\n| Dresser | Wooden Table + Dungeon Door |\n| Bookshelf | Wooden Crate + Wooden BG |\n| Lattice BG | Wooden Chair + Wooden BG |\n| Window | Glass Pane + Wooden BG |\n| Bed | Wooden Chair + Agaric Mushroom |\n| Toilet | White + Dirt |\n| Bathtub | Toilet + White |\n| Plumbing | Bathtub + Green |\n| Treasure Chest | Golden Block + Dresser |\n\n### Colour blocks\n| You get | Splice these two |\n|---|---|\n| Red | Brick Block + Magma |\n| Orange | Red + Yellow |\n| Yellow | Brick Block + Daisy |\n| Green | Brick Block + Grass |\n| Lime | Green + Grass |\n| Blue | Brick Block + Cornflower |\n| Cyan | Blue + Grass |\n| Light Blue | Blue + Glass Pane |\n| Purple | Red + Blue |\n| Magenta | Purple + Glass Pane |\n| Pink | Red + Glass Pane |\n| Brown | Brick Block + Dirt |\n| Black | Brick Block + Dirt BG |\n| White | Brick Block + Agaric Mushroom |\n| Rainbow | Purple + Orange |\n\n### Glass, metal and light\n| You get | Splice these two |\n|---|---|\n| Glass Block | Sand + Magma |\n| Glass Pane | Stone + Magma |\n| Amber Glass | Dirt + Glass Pane |\n| Torch | Wooden Sign + Magma |\n| Pocket Lighter | Torch + Dark Aqua Block |\n| Lantern | Torch + Glass Pane |\n| Lamp Post | Neon Lights + Plumbing |\n| Gold Chain | Climbing Vine + Golden Block |\n| Golden Block | Steel Block + Yellow |\n| Steel Block | Portcullis + Purple |\n| Steel Girder | Steel Block + Lattice BG |\n| Iron Block | Tesla Coil + Magenta |\n| Tesla Coil | Glass Spike + Blue |\n| Glass Spike | Cactus + Glass Pane |\n| Acid | Cactus + Plumbing |\n| Ruby Block | Crystal Block + Slumber Marble Block |\n| Emerald Block | Crystal Block + Acid |\n| Slumber Marble Block | Bed + Orange |\n| Evil Bricks | Magma + Black |\n| Fireplace | Evil Bricks + Golden Block |\n| Chandelier | Golden Block + Fireplace |\n\n### Doors, buildings and signs\n| You get | Splice these two |\n|---|---|\n| Dungeon Door | Wooden Door + Window |\n| House Entrance | Dungeon Door + Wooden Door |\n| Tenement Building | House Entrance + Garbage |\n| Western Building | Tenement Building + Sand |\n| Cutaway Building | Western Building + Tenement Building |\n| Neon Outline Block | Neon Lights + Cutaway Building |\n| Pointer Sign | Wooden Door + Wooden Sign |\n| Danger Sign | Pointer Sign + Magma |\n| Death Spikes | Danger Sign + Stone BG |\n| Portcullis | Dungeon Door + Death Spikes |\n| Bumper | Magma + Red |\n| Checkpoint | Bed + Rainbow |\n| Devil Horns | Death Spikes + Magma |\n\n### Appliances and music\n| You get | Splice these two |\n|---|---|\n| Kitchen Oven | Pocket Lighter + Air Duct |\n| Microwave | Toxic Waste Barrel + Television |\n| Boombox | Black + Steel Block |\n| Disco Ball | Boombox + Window |\n\n### Wallpaper and wings\n| You get | Splice these two |\n|---|---|\n| Sizzling Bacon Wallpaper | Rainbow + House Entrance |\n| Red Wallpaper | Sizzling Bacon Wallpaper + Red |\n| Blue Wallpaper | Sizzling Bacon Wallpaper + Blue |\n| Flowery Wallpaper | Wooden BG + Daisy |\n| Fairy Wings | Flowery Wallpaper + Disco Ball |\n| Crimson Eagle Wings | Red Wallpaper + Blue Wallpaper |\n| Rainbow Wings | Ruby Block + Emerald Block |\n\n### Seeds you will not splice\nThese seeds are used in recipes but are not the result of one, so you have to find them. The seed packs in the Store and the theme packs are the usual places. See [How to get things](#how-to-get-things).\n\nAir Duct, Bush, Climbing Vine, Cloudstone Block, Crystal Block, Dark Aqua Block, Dirt, Dirt BG, Garbage, Giant Up Arrow, Gravel, Magma, Neon Lights, Stone, Television, Toxic Waste Barrel.\n\n### Halloween splices\nThese only work while the Halloween event is on.\n\n| You get | Splice these two |\n|---|---|\n| Pumpkin | Sunflower + Dirt |\n| Jack-o'-Lantern | Pumpkin + Torch |\n| Tombstone | Stone + Cave Gateway |\n| Cobweb | Glass Pane + Wooden Frame |\n| Haunted BG | Dirt BG + Purple |\n\n## Chemical Combiner\nWrench a **Laboratory** or a **Microwave**, add up to three kinds of chemical in **exact** amounts, and mix. A wrong mix **destroys** everything you put in, so check this table first.\n\n| You make | Mix |\n|---|---|\n| Mysterious Chemical | 20 Chemical Y, 10 Chemical B, 5 Chemical P |\n| Lab Coat | 10 Chemical R, 3 Chemical Y, 3 Chemical P |\n| Lab Goggles | 2 Chemical R, 4 Chemical B, 3 Chemical P |\n| Electrified Hair | 30 Chemical G, 4 Chemical R, 1 Chemical B |\n| {{icon:item-voltjack}} Voltjack (makes 3) | 10 Chemical G, 5 Chemical R, 1 Chemical P |\n| Forcefield | 20 Chemical G, 10 Chemical R, 1 Mysterious Chemical |\n\n## Harvest Festival combines\nWhile the festival runs, mooncakes drop from harvested trees. Bake these in a **Kitchen Oven** by dropping in the ingredients and punching it to shut the door. The game prints these four recipes on the items themselves.\n\n| You make | Ingredients |\n|---|---|\n| {{icon:item-moonlight-mooncake}} Moonlight Mooncake | 2 Golden Yolk, 10 Lotus and 10 Red Bean Mooncakes |\n| {{icon:item-songpyeon}} Songpyeon | 2 Moonlight, 4 Lotus and 4 Red Bean Mooncakes |\n| {{icon:item-hand-scythe}} Hand Scythe | 2 Songpyeon, 4 Lotus and 4 Red Bean Mooncakes (festival only) |\n| Zeus' Thunderbolt | 20 Songpyeon, 20 Golden Yolk and 20 Lotus Mooncakes |\n\nOther festival recipes are not listed. The Gazette hints at them.\n"},"farming-and-splicing":{"title":"Farming and Splicing","nav":"Farming and splicing","summary":"Plant a seed, wait, punch the ripe tree, and collect the blocks it grows. Splice two seeds to make a new kind of tree.","md":"# Farming and Splicing\n\nPlant a seed, wait, punch the ripe tree, and collect the blocks it grows. Splice two seeds to make a new kind of tree.\n\n## Planting and harvesting\n1. Select a seed and use it on an empty tile **directly above a solid block**.\n2. Wait for the tree to finish growing. It shows a growth timer.\n3. Select your **Fist** and punch the ripe tree to harvest it.\n4. Walk over the drops to collect them. Keep some seeds to plant again.\n\nPunching a tree that has not finished growing removes it early, so wait for it to ripen.\n\n## Trees now look different\n\n<!--fig-trees-->\n<figure class=\"fig\" aria-label=\"The 12 kinds of tree\">\n<p class=\"fig-title\">The 12 kinds of tree (ripe, with an example seed)</p>\n<div class=\"gallery\">\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:tree-palm}}<b>Palm</b><span>Palm Tree Seed</span></div>\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:tree-pine}}<b>Pine</b><span>Sequoia Tree Seed</span></div>\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:tree-cactus}}<b>Cactus</b><span>Cactus Seed</span></div>\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:tree-mushroom}}<b>Mushroom</b><span>Agaric Mushroom Seed</span></div>\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:tree-crystal}}<b>Crystal</b><span>Glass Block Seed</span></div>\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:tree-willow}}<b>Willow</b><span>Leaves Seed</span></div>\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:tree-blossom}}<b>Blossom</b><span>Sunflower Seed</span></div>\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:tree-oak}}<b>Oak</b><span>Wooden Block Seed</span></div>\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:tree-poplar}}<b>Poplar</b><span>Dirt Seed</span></div>\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:tree-bush}}<b>Bush</b><span>Dirt BG Seed</span></div>\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:tree-bare}}<b>Bare</b><span>Tombstone Seed</span></div>\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:tree-block}}<b>Block</b><span>Stone Seed</span></div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"fig-note\">Leaves take the colour of the seed, so two seeds of the same kind can look different.</p>\n</figure>\n\nSeeds used to all grow the same tree. There are now **12 kinds of tree**: palm, pine, cactus, mushroom, crystal, willow, blossom, oak, poplar, bush, a spooky bare tree and a blocky stone tree. The item the seed grows decides which kind you get.\n- A ripe tree shows one icon of the item it gives, with a small badge for how many you will get.\n- Ripe trees sparkle with a gold twinkle.\n- A tree made by splicing shows its result from the young stage, so you can see what it will give.\n\n## Splicing: making new seeds\n\n<!--fig-splice-->\n<figure class=\"fig fig-flow\" aria-label=\"Splicing steps\">\n<p class=\"fig-title\">Splicing in three steps</p>\n<div class=\"fig-row\">\n<div class=\"step\">{{icon:item-dirt-seed}}<b>Plant a seed</b><span>Put the first seed in the ground.</span></div>\n<div class=\"step\">{{icon:item-blackrock-wall-seed}}<b>Add a second seed</b><span>While the tree grows, use another seed on the same tree.</span></div>\n<div class=\"step\">{{icon:tree-oak}}<b>Harvest the new tree</b><span>A compatible pair grows something new.</span></div>\n</div>\n</figure>\n\n1. Plant a seed.\n2. While that tree is still growing, select a **second seed** and use it on the **same tree**.\n3. A compatible pair becomes a new tree. Wait for it to grow and harvest as usual.\n\nSeeds combine on a growing tree, not in your inventory. In the tutorial you splice a Magma seed with a Dirt seed to get Wooden Blocks, and later a Wooden Block seed with a Dirt seed to grow Cargo Shorts.\n\nEvery splice recipe is listed on [Recipes](#recipes). The **Seed Diary** in the side menu lists splices you have found. New seeds are worth more to other players, so splice everything you can.\n\n## Good first seeds\n| Pack | Price | What you get |\n|---|---|---|\n| Basic Seed Pack | 100 gems | 5 random common seeds |\n| Basic Splicing Kit | 150 gems | 5 random starter seeds for your first splices |\n| Rare Seed Pack | 1,000 gems | 5 random seeds from over 120 rare kinds |\n| Starter Farmables Pack | 3,000 gems, one per day | 6 random bundles of 6 seeds: Sugar Cane, Blackrock Wall, Venus Flytrap, Fish Tank |\n\n- **Blackrock Wall** takes about 1 hour 45 minutes to grow and **Sugar Cane** about 4 hours, so they make good first farms.\n- **Venus Flytrap** and **Fish Tank** take most of a day but pay more gems per block.\n- Save 2,000 gems for a World Lock first so your farm is safe, then buy the Starter Farmables Pack.\n\n## Farmer's Illness\n\n<!--fig-illness-->\n<figure class=\"fig\" aria-label=\"Farmer's Illness over time\">\n<p class=\"fig-title\">Rewards over one farming session</p>\n<div class=\"meter\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Full rewards for 2 hours, then falling to 5 percent by 2 hours 45 minutes\">\n<i class=\"m-good\" style=\"width:66.7%\"></i><i class=\"m-fade\" style=\"width:25%\"></i><i class=\"m-warn\" style=\"width:8.3%\"></i>\n</div>\n<div class=\"meter-key\"><span>0 to 2 hours: full rewards</span><span class=\"k-fade\">2 to 2 hours 45: falling fast</span><span class=\"k-warn\">After that: about 5%</span></div>\n<p class=\"fig-note\">A 15 minute break cures it. Only active farming counts, so a gap of more than a minute adds nothing.</p>\n</figure>\n\nFarming without a break wears you out, so rewards fade the longer you farm.\n- You get **full rewards for about 2 hours** of active farming.\n- After that rewards drop quickly and bottom out at about **2 hours 45 minutes**.\n- A **15 minute break** cures it. Hopping between worlds does not reset it.\n- Only active farming counts. If you stop for more than a minute, that gap adds nothing.\n- Warning icons show how worn out you are, and other players in the world can see it.\n\nIt also thins out drops from the Hand Scythe, Riding Cloud rain and festival mooncakes, so plan a break instead of farming all evening.\n\n## Growing faster\n| Item | What it does | Price |\n|---|---|---|\n| {{icon:item-growth-mist}} Growth Mist | Each bottle removes one hour of growth from a tree. Sold in fives. | 200 gems for 5 |\n| {{icon:item-deluxe-growth-mist}} Deluxe Growth Mist | Removes 24 hours of growth from a tree. | 900 gems |\n| {{icon:item-hand-scythe}} Hand Scythe | Harvesting trees below rarity 100 gives double fruit. It can snap, so carry a spare. | See the Store |\n| {{icon:item-farm-tractor}} Farm Tractor | Ride it to harvest ripe trees you drive through. Comes in the Farm Pack. | 15,000 gems (Farm Pack) |\n| Riding Cloud | When full, it rains on the first three growing trees you pass and makes them grow a little faster. Refills after about 30 minutes. | See Storms in Worlds and Building |\n\nA tree can only be watered by the cloud once, so it never stacks.\n\n## Tips\n- Lock first, farm second. Anything on unlocked land can be harvested or broken by visitors.\n- Plant in rows with a block under each tree. Trees only grow above a solid block.\n- Daily missions often ask for planting and harvesting, so farm while you complete them.\n"},"fishing":{"title":"Fishing","nav":"Fishing","summary":"Cast a line into water, hold on through the reel, and sell or keep what you catch.","md":"# Fishing\n\nCast a line into water, hold on through the reel, and sell or keep what you catch.\n\n## How to fish\n\n<!--fig-cast-->\n<figure class=\"fig fig-flow\" aria-label=\"Fishing in four steps\">\n<p class=\"fig-title\">One cast, start to finish</p>\n<div class=\"fig-row\">\n<div class=\"step\">{{icon:rod-fishing-rod}}<b>Wear a rod</b><span>It goes in your hand slot.</span></div>\n<div class=\"step\">{{icon:bait-worm-bait}}<b>Pick a bait</b><span>Select it in your quickbar.</span></div>\n<div class=\"step\">{{icon:fish-minnow}}<b>Cast on water</b><span>A pool at least 2 by 2 tiles. Stand on the ground.</span></div>\n<div class=\"step\">{{icon:item-fishing-token}}<b>Reel it in</b><span>On FISH ON!, hold to keep the fish in the green zone.</span></div>\n</div>\n</figure>\n\n1. **Wear a rod** (it goes in your hand slot) and pick a **bait** in your quickbar.\n2. Find water that is part of a pool **at least 2 tiles wide and 2 tiles deep**, and stand on the ground.\n3. Use the bait on the water to cast.\n4. When you see **FISH ON!**, hold to lift the green zone and keep the fish inside it until the reel fills. Stay near your bobber or the line snaps.\n\n- A fish heavier than your rod's line limit always snaps the line.\n- Every cast wears the rod. You get a warning at 25 casts left and again at 10. Repair it at a Fishing Hut for gems.\n- Fishing time adds up. After about **1.5 hours** of fishing you get seasick and cannot fish for 30 minutes. A 30 minute break clears it.\n- Messages in a Bottle hide gems inside. Double-click one to read it.\n\n## Fishing Hut\n\n<!--fig-hut-->\n<figure class=\"fig fig-flow\" aria-label=\"Fishing Hut upgrades\">\n<p class=\"fig-title\">Hut upgrade ladder (World Locks)</p>\n<div class=\"fig-row\">\n<div class=\"step\">{{icon:item-fishing-hut}}<b>Butcher</b><span>1 World Lock</span></div>\n<div class=\"step\">{{icon:item-pearl}}<b>Appraiser</b><span>3 World Locks</span></div>\n<div class=\"step\">{{icon:item-fishing-token}}<b>Smuggler and Gacha</b><span>8 World Locks</span></div>\n<div class=\"step\">{{icon:item-world-lock}}<b>Line Insurance</b><span>20 World Locks</span></div>\n</div>\n</figure>\n\nBuy a **Fishing Hut** (1,000 gems) or the **Fishin' Pack** (3,000 gems: a Hut, a rod, bait, a Fishbowl and a Fish Tank Port). Place the hut, then wrench it. Breaking the hut puts it back in your backpack, and its upgrades stay with you.\n\n| Upgrade | Cost | Adds |\n|---|---|---|\n| Butcher | 1 World Lock | Fillet fish into crafting materials and craft hybrid blocks |\n| Appraiser | 3 World Locks | Reroll a fish's mutation for gems and 1 World Lock |\n| Smuggler and Bait Gacha | 8 World Locks | The Smuggler visits for 15 minutes now and then to trade rare gear, and the Bait and Chum Gacha opens |\n| Line Insurance | 20 World Locks | One second chance when your line snaps on an Epic, Legendary or Boss catch |\n\nThe Hut also has a **Gear Shop**, a **Fish Market** where you sell fish, and a **Workbench** for crafting and rod repair.\n\n## Rods\n**Lure Speed** shortens the wait for a bite. **Luck** raises your chances of rarer fish and heavier weights. **Line** is the heaviest fish the line can hold.\n\n| Rod | Lure Speed | Luck | Line | What it does |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| {{icon:rod-fishing-rod}} Fishing Rod | 12% | 10% | 20 kg | A plain starter rod |\n| {{icon:rod-bamboo-rod}} Bamboo | 13% | 14% | 30 kg | More XP from Common and Uncommon fish |\n| {{icon:rod-driftwood-rod}} Driftwood | 14% | 22% | 40 kg | Junk can wash up a free bait |\n| {{icon:rod-reinforced-iron-rod}} Reinforced Iron | 15% | 40% | 75 kg | Sturdy Line: less tension while reeling |\n| {{icon:rod-lucky-clover-rod}} Lucky Clover | 14% | 50% | 60 kg | Sometimes keeps your bait; can catch Rainbow fish |\n| {{icon:rod-coral-reef-rod}} Coral Reef | 19% | 38% | 85 kg | Can catch Neon fish; Undersea fish bite more |\n| {{icon:rod-golden-rod}} Golden | 21% | 60% | 100 kg | Often catches Golden fish |\n| {{icon:rod-sunken-brass-rod}} Sunken Brass | 22% | 70% | 150 kg | Can catch Diamond fish and bring up a Pearl |\n| {{icon:rod-frostline-rod}} Frostline | 23% | 55% | 110 kg | Can catch Frozen fish; Deep Freeze can freeze a fish mid-reel |\n| {{icon:rod-cursed-fishing-rod}} Cursed | 23% | 150% | 250 kg | Makes mutations more likely |\n| {{icon:rod-magma-core-rod}} Magma Core | 18% | 95% | 180 kg | Can catch Magma fish; Mars fish pay more tokens |\n| {{icon:rod-storm-weaver-rod}} Storm-Weaver | 28% | 80% | 120 kg | Stronger in storms; can open a Storm Pool |\n| {{icon:rod-trench-stalker-rod}} Trench-Stalker | 32% | 110% | 220 kg | Can catch Toxic fish; abyss fish bite twice as often |\n| {{icon:rod-abyssal-warden-rod}} Abyssal Warden | 36% | 140% | 350 kg | Junk never bites; bosses and void fish fight a little less |\n| {{icon:rod-abyssal-overlord-rod}} Abyssal Overlord | 42% | 175% | 400 kg | Can catch Void fish and sometimes a second fish |\n\nReach **Fishing Level 10** to earn a Golden Rod. Some rods are only sold or traded in special ways: the Smuggler has rods you cannot buy, and the Cursed Rod comes from Gorlock during Halloween.\n\n## Baits\n| Bait | Effect |\n|---|---|\n| {{icon:bait-worm-bait}} Worm | +5% Lure Speed |\n| {{icon:bait-shrimp-lure}} Shrimp | +12% Luck |\n| {{icon:bait-glowing-lure}} Glowing Lure | +15% Luck |\n| {{icon:bait-chum-bucket}} Chum Bucket | −10% Lure Speed; sharks are twice as likely |\n| {{icon:bait-heavy-pellet-bait}} Heavy Pellet | +15% Resilience, −5% Lure Speed |\n| World baits | Static Grub (storm), Ember Larva (Mars), Jungle Beetle, Krill Cluster. Sold in packs of 10, and also dug up in their world. |\n| Mutation baits | Frost Fly (Frozen), Golden Grub (Golden and Goldfish), Prism Lure (all colours, from the Gacha) |\n| Rare baits | Thunderhead Minnow, Molten Heart, Sacred Grub, Siren Pearl Lure, Koi Blossom, Blood Chum. These cannot be bought and each boosts named Epic and Legendary fish. |\n\nTwo of them you can craft at the Workbench: **Molten Heart** (a Magma-Core Shark plus 40 Magma Crust) and **Blood Chum** (a Shark plus 10 Abyssal Essence).\n\n## Fish and where they live\n\n<!--fig-fish-->\n<figure class=\"fig\" aria-label=\"Fish by rarity and where they live\">\n<p class=\"fig-title\">From Common to Boss (base sell price)</p>\n<div class=\"hbars\">\n<div class=\"hrow\"><div class=\"nm\">{{icon:fish-minnow}}Common</div><div class=\"track\"><i style=\"width:1%\"></i></div><div class=\"val\">36 gems</div></div>\n<div class=\"hrow\"><div class=\"nm\">{{icon:fish-trout}}Uncommon</div><div class=\"track\"><i style=\"width:1%\"></i></div><div class=\"val\">40 gems</div></div>\n<div class=\"hrow\"><div class=\"nm\">{{icon:fish-salmon}}Rare</div><div class=\"track\"><i style=\"width:2%\"></i></div><div class=\"val\">81 gems</div></div>\n<div class=\"hrow\"><div class=\"nm\">{{icon:fish-koi}}Epic</div><div class=\"track\"><i style=\"width:30%\"></i></div><div class=\"val\">1,215 gems</div></div>\n<div class=\"hrow\"><div class=\"nm\">{{icon:fish-golden}}Legendary</div><div class=\"track\"><i style=\"width:100%\"></i></div><div class=\"val\">4,050 gems</div></div>\n<div class=\"hrow\"><div class=\"nm\">{{icon:fish-royal_kraken}}Boss</div><div class=\"track\"><i style=\"width:99%\"></i></div><div class=\"val\">4,000 gems</div></div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"fig-note\">Base price before weight and mutation. Bars are to scale, so the Common to Rare fish are tiny next to Epic and above.</p>\n<p class=\"fig-title\" style=\"margin-top:18px\">Where to find them</p>\n<div class=\"gallery\">\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:fish-bass}}<b>Ordinary water</b><span>Bass</span></div>\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:fish-gale_carp}}<b>Storm worlds</b><span>Gale Carp</span></div>\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:fish-magma_chub}}<b>Mars</b><span>Magma Basin Chub</span></div>\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:fish-bog_piranha}}<b>Jungle</b><span>Bog Piranha</span></div>\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:fish-coral_damselfish}}<b>Undersea</b><span>Coral Damselfish</span></div>\n<div class=\"tile\">{{icon:fish-abyssal_viperfish}}<b>The Abyss</b><span>Abyssal Viperfish</span></div>\n</div>\n</figure>\n\n- **Rarity:** Common, Uncommon, Rare, Epic, Legendary and Boss.\n- **Habitats:** ordinary water, Storm worlds, Mars, Jungle, Undersea and the Abyss.\n- **Fish Index:** open it to see every fish with where it lives, the best bait, its weight range, your best catch and its sell price. Fish you have not caught yet show as a dark silhouette under a padlock. Filter by habitat, rarity or Caught and Missing.\n- **Cutscenes:** Legendary and Boss catches play a full cutscene on the angler's screen, and everyone in the world sees the creature.\n\n### Mutations\nA fish can come up with a **colour**, and separately a **size**. A fish has at most one colour. The rarer the colour, the more it is worth.\n- **Colours:** Golden, Albino, Electric (more likely in storms), Void (inside an Abyssal Void), Frozen, Toxic, Neon, Magma, Diamond, Rainbow, Error, Cosmic and Celestial.\n- **Sizes:** Tiny (worth less), Fat and Huge.\n- Colour mutations and Huge fish play a special effect when they come up.\n\n## Selling\nThe Fish Market pays by weight: the lightest fish of its kind sells for half the usual price and the heaviest for one and a half times.\n\n| Rarity | Base price before weight and mutation |\n|---|---|\n| Common | 36 gems |\n| Uncommon | 40 gems |\n| Rare | 81 gems |\n| Epic | 1,215 gems |\n| Legendary | 4,050 gems |\n| Boss | 4,000 gems |\n\nPrices can change with updates. Fish also drop **Fishing Tokens**, rarer fish more often, which you spend in the Fishing Exchange.\n\n## Abyssal Voids\nIn Undersea worlds a patch of water can turn into an **Abyssal Void** for about 10 minutes. Only abyss fish bite there, and everything you catch is a Void fish. Some voids hold a boss, a Colossal Megalodon or Neptune's Royal Kraken. Once a boss is landed it leaves that world for about 6 hours. A very rare catch, the **Abyssal Void Contract**, lets you open a void in any world with water. Double-click it to sign.\n\n## Rides\nBig fish such as the Megalodon can be trained in a **Fish Tank** by feeding them other fish, then ridden on land. A fully trained Megalodon makes you about 35% faster on land. Only a Cursed Rod can hook a Megalodon.\n"},"gems-and-trading":{"title":"Gems and Trading","nav":"Gems and trading","summary":"Gems are the everyday money. World Locks are the money for big trades.","md":"# Gems and Trading\n\nGems are the everyday money. World Locks are the money for big trades.\n\n## Currencies\n\n<!--fig-money-->\n<figure class=\"fig fig-flow\" aria-label=\"Gems, World Locks and Diamond Locks\">\n<p class=\"fig-title\">How the money fits together</p>\n<div class=\"fig-row\">\n<div class=\"step\">{{icon:gem}}<b>Gems</b><span>Everyday money from play and the Store.</span></div>\n<div class=\"step\">{{icon:item-world-lock}}<b>World Lock</b><span>2,000 gems in the Store.</span></div>\n<div class=\"step\">{{icon:item-diamond-lock}}<b>Diamond Lock</b><span>100 World Locks.</span></div>\n</div>\n</figure>\n\n- **Gems:** earned by breaking blocks, harvesting, missions, level-ups and daily rewards. Spend them in the Store.\n- **World Lock:** worth 2,000 gems in the Store. Players use World Locks to price items and settle trades.\n- **Diamond Lock:** worth 100 World Locks.\n\n## Spending gems\n| Item | Price |\n|---|---|\n| World Lock | 2,000 gems |\n| Backpack space (+10 slots per upgrade, up to 396) | 100, then 200, 500, 1,000, 1,700 gems, then it keeps rising |\n| Treasure Chest | 500 gems |\n| Vending Machine | 8,000 gems |\n| Seed Vending Machine | 500 gems |\n\n## Buying gems with Robux\n\n<!--fig-packs-->\n<figure class=\"fig\" aria-label=\"Gem pack value\">\n<p class=\"fig-title\">Gems per Robux, by pack</p>\n<div class=\"hbars\">\n<div class=\"hrow\"><div class=\"nm\">{{icon:gem}}Pocket Sparkle</div><div class=\"track\"><i style=\"width:30.5%\"></i></div><div class=\"val\">16.8</div></div>\n<div class=\"hrow\"><div class=\"nm\">{{icon:gem}}Gem Pouch</div><div class=\"track\"><i style=\"width:45.6%\"></i></div><div class=\"val\">25.1</div></div>\n<div class=\"hrow\"><div class=\"nm\">{{icon:gem}}Gem Barrel</div><div class=\"track\"><i style=\"width:60.7%\"></i></div><div class=\"val\">33.4</div></div>\n<div class=\"hrow\"><div class=\"nm\">{{icon:gem}}Treasure Chest</div><div class=\"track\"><i style=\"width:82.7%\"></i></div><div class=\"val\">45.5</div></div>\n<div class=\"hrow\"><div class=\"nm\">{{icon:gem}}Mine Cart Haul</div><div class=\"track\"><i style=\"width:90.9%\"></i></div><div class=\"val\">50.0</div></div>\n<div class=\"hrow\"><div class=\"nm\">{{icon:gem}}Gem Throne</div><div class=\"track\"><i style=\"width:100%\"></i></div><div class=\"val\">55.0</div></div>\n</div>\n</figure>\n\n| Pack | Gems | Robux | Gems per Robux |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Pocket Sparkle | 2,500 | 149 | 16.8 |\n| Gem Pouch | 10,000 | 399 | 25.1 |\n| Gem Barrel | 50,000 | 1,499 | 33.4 |\n| Treasure Chest | 150,000 | 3,300 | 45.5 |\n| Mine Cart Haul | 350,000 | 7,000 | 50.0 |\n| Gem Throne | 550,000 | 10,000 | 55.0 |\n\nThe bigger the pack, the better the value. Supporter passes add a bonus on top.\n\n## Supporter passes and the Starter Pack\n| | Cost | What you get |\n|---|---|---|\n| Starter Pack | 30 Robux | A World Lock, an outfit, 10 extra backpack slots and a 5% gem pack bonus |\n| Supporter | 1,000 Robux | 40 extra backpack slots, 50,000 gems, +10% on gem packs, extra skin colours, more XP |\n| Super Supporter | 2,500 Robux | 100 extra backpack slots, 150,000 gems, +20% on gem packs, extra skin colours, more XP |\n| Upgrade to Super Supporter | 1,500 Robux | For Supporter owners |\n\nPasses are permanent, and Super includes everything in Supporter.\n\n## Gifting\nYou can buy a gem pack, a Supporter pass or the Starter Pack **for another player**. Pick the player in the gift menu. The gift arrives right away if they are here, or waits in their gift box. Gifts cannot be undone, and you cannot gift something the player already owns.\n\n## Trading\n\n<!--fig-trade-->\n<figure class=\"fig fig-flow\" aria-label=\"How a trade works\">\n<p class=\"fig-title\">A trade in four steps</p>\n<div class=\"fig-row\">\n<div class=\"step\">{{icon:item-backpack}}<b>Wrench the player</b><span>Choose Trade. You both need level 10.</span></div>\n<div class=\"step\">{{icon:item-treasure-chest}}<b>Offer items</b><span>Four slots each. Tap a slot, pick an item and amount.</span></div>\n<div class=\"step\">{{icon:item-pearl}}<b>Both Accept</b><span>Read the review screen: what you give and get.</span></div>\n<div class=\"step\">{{icon:item-world-lock}}<b>Do The Trade!</b><span>If anything changes, accepts reset.</span></div>\n</div>\n</figure>\n\nYou need to reach **level 10** to trade, and trades have extra account checks to stop scams.\n1. Select the **Wrench**, use it on another player in the same world and choose **Trade**.\n2. Each side has **4 slots**. Tap a slot, pick an item and an amount.\n3. Both players press **Accept**. A review screen lists exactly what you give and what you get.\n4. Press **Do The Trade!** to finish.\n\n- If either offer changes, you see **The deal changed!** and both accepts reset. Read it again.\n- Giving a **World Key** makes the other player the owner of that world. The review warns you.\n- Tools and untradeable items cannot be traded.\n- **Dropping items on the floor is not a trade.** Anyone can pick them up.\n\n## Vending machines\n- A **Vending Machine** sells one kind of item, priced in World Locks. A **Seed Vending Machine** is priced in a seed you choose.\n- You need to reach the trade level to stock a machine. Tools, gems, locks and untradeable items cannot be sold.\n- Collect your earnings from the machine. Diamond Locks come out first, then World Locks.\n- A Signal Jammer in your world hides it from public listings.\n\n## Auctions\nOpen **Auctions** from the Menu.\n- Lots last about 6 hours and are chosen by the game's owner.\n- You bid with World Locks (a Diamond Lock counts as 100).\n- **If you are outbid, your bid is refunded in full.** Collect refunds and prizes from the auction window.\n- **Winning bids are final.**\n- Opening an auction cancels a trade you have open.\n\n## Staying safe\n- Use the trade window every time.\n- Do not give items away for a promise.\n- Check the exact items and amounts before you accept.\n- If you think someone scammed you, report them from the player menu, and also use Report in the Roblox menu.\n"},"events":{"title":"Events","nav":"Events","summary":"Seasonal events change what you can find and make. The in-game Gazette (the Events button) says what is running now.","md":"# Events\n\nSeasonal events change what you can find and make. The in-game **Gazette** (the Events button) says what is running now.\n\n## Harvest Festival\nThe festival runs through **November**.\n- **Mooncakes:** while it runs, harvesting trees can drop mooncakes. The rarer the tree, the better the loot. Farmer's Illness thins mooncake drops, so take breaks.\n- **Missions:** a Harvest Festival set of missions appears in your Missions list.\n- **Festival cooking:** harvest foods and some items can only be made during the festival. Their recipes are hints in the game, so experiment. See [Recipes](#recipes) for the combines the game spells out.\n- **Songpyeon Event:** every so often a world with players in it gets 3 Songpyeons dropped on open tiles, on the ground or floating in the air. Find them within **30 seconds** and you keep them.\n- **Sky Lanterns:** release one during the festival and make a wish. Rarely, a Lunar Dragon Heart drifts down, with a fireworks scene for everyone in the world.\n- **Harvest board:** harvests during the festival count toward a leaderboard. When it ends, the top players of that festival get the **Harvest Champion** title.\n\n### The Offering Table\nWrench an **Offering Table** and offer mooncakes to the harvest moon for one random reward. Rarer mooncakes roll from a better pool.\n\n<figure class=\"fig fig-flow\" aria-label=\"Offering Table tiers\">\n<p class=\"fig-title\">Three tiers</p>\n<div class=\"fig-row\">\n<div class=\"step \">{{icon:item-lotus-mooncake}}<b>Common</b><span>25 Lotus or 25 Red Bean Mooncakes per offering.</span></div>\n<div class=\"step \">{{icon:item-golden-yolk-mooncake}}<b>Rare</b><span>3 Golden Yolk Mooncakes per offering.</span></div>\n<div class=\"step \">{{icon:item-moonlight-mooncake}}<b>Legendary</b><span>2 Moonlight Mooncakes per offering.</span></div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"fig-note\">The Offering Table shows the exact chances for each reward before you offer.</p>\n</figure>\n\nRewards include:\n- {{icon:item-paper-lantern}} Paper Lanterns\n- {{icon:item-golden-yolk-mooncake}} Golden Yolk and Moonlight Mooncakes\n- {{icon:item-sakura-kimono}} Kimonos\n- {{icon:item-harvest-scythe}} The Harvest Scythe\n- {{icon:item-autumns-royal-crown}} Autumn's Royal Crown\n- {{icon:item-autumns-royal-cape}} Autumn's Royal Cape\n- {{icon:item-fall-kings-robe}} Fall King's and Fall Queen's Robes\n\n### Harvest Scythe\nWear it and harvesting trees below rarity 100 sometimes gives an extra seed. It never breaks. The ordinary **Hand Scythe** gives double fruit instead but can snap.\n\n## Halloween\nWhile Halloween runs, spooky **Gorlock** castle worlds open. Gorlock takes offerings and gives rewards.\n- **Offerings:** bring spare blocks, seeds or clothes you are not wearing. Choose an item and an amount and the game shows you the full list of possible rewards and their chances **before** anything is used up. Higher-rarity offerings unlock more rewards.\n- **Special exchanges:** Gorlock also swaps sets of items for stagewear, dinosaur outfits, capes, a Reaper Scythe and more. Each exchange shows exactly what it needs.\n- **Bat Wing Tatters:** dig underground during the event to find them. They are traded for Bat Wings.\n- **Block transformations:** turn spare blocks into Halloween building pieces.\n- **Castle hazards:** watching eyes, snapping jaws and roaming minions guard the castle. Stay on the path.\n\n## WinterFest\nWhen WinterFest runs, a **WINTERFEST** world opens with a **Nutcracker** who trades winter items for World Locks. It only trades while the event is on.\n\n## Seasonal fun\n- **Gazette:** open the Events button for each month's banner and news.\n- **Missions:** look for seasonal sets in Missions.\n"},"whats-new":{"title":"What's New","nav":"What's new","summary":"The latest changes to Own A World, newest first.","md":"# What's New\n\nThe latest changes to Own A World, newest first.\n\n## 18 November 2026\n### 12 new kinds of tree\nEvery seed tree used to look the same. Now your seed decides the tree: palm, pine, cactus, mushroom, crystal, willow, blossom, oak, poplar, bush, a spooky bare tree and a blocky stone tree.\n- Ripe trees show the item they give, with a small badge for how many you will get.\n- Ripe trees sparkle with a gold twinkle.\n- A spliced tree shows its result from the young stage.\n\nSee [Farming and splicing](#farming-and-splicing).\n\n### Fish swim\n33 fish are now animated, including their colour mutations.\n\n### Bubble Wings reworked\nBubbles flow out along each feather and pop at the tip, and the wings are bigger.\n\n### Fishing and Harvest Festival update\n- **Rods** now have **Lure Speed** and signature traits, such as extra mutation chances, double catches and freezing a fish mid-reel.\n- **New baits:** world baits, mutation baits and rare baits for Epic and Legendary fish.\n- **13 fish colour mutations** plus Tiny, Fat and Huge sizes, each with its own catch effect.\n- **Legendary and Boss catches** play a full cutscene.\n- **Fish Index:** see every fish, where it lives, the best bait and your best catch.\n- **Abyssal Void Contract:** a very rare catch that opens an Abyssal Void in any world with water.\n- **Harvest Festival** is on all November. See [Events](#events).\n\nSee [Fishing](#fishing).\n\n### World Honors\nWorlds are ranked by how many different players visit. Use /top and /honors. See [Commands](#commands).\n\n### Storms and Sky Lanterns\nStorm worlds now strike the highest player with lightning every so often. A lucky strike on someone carrying a Sky Bottle turns it into a Riding Cloud. Sky Lanterns can drop the Lunar Dragon Heart with a fireworks scene.\n\nSpotted something odd? Tell us in the game's Discord, with the world name and what you were doing.\n"}}};
